              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sarah Jo"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is one of my favorite ways to eat asparagus. I do add one clove of minced garlic to the mix before I roast the asparagus. This is also just as good cold."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "courtney_r12"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Would make again. Only made a half recipe, added 2 cloves garlic chopped thin and tossed. Baked for 8 mins then added balsamic and baked for 2 more. Came out nice and crunchy with good flavor and family enjoyed. I used a small pyrex roasting pan so not sure if that made the difference as I saw others say it came out mushy.",
            "datePublished": "2016-02-27T03:45:19.040Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Katy Wright"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Such a simple and great way to prepare asparagus. I always add a couple of cloves of chopped garlic along with the oil and S&amp;P. I drizzle some balsamic on the asparagus for the last 5 min of cooking, and then add a bit of extra thick balsamic when I serve it - either the fancy thick expensive stuff, or I make a quick stovetop reduction with a tiny sprinkle of sugar on top. Always a favourite!",
            "datePublished": "2014-02-04T13:32:44.573Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "melissa master cavell"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I gave this 5 stars for ease of preparation and great taste. I dusted it with a little garlic powder, and sprayed it with olive oil rather than drizzle the oil. Everyone at the table had seconds and there was none left at the end of the meal. Thanks for the great &amp; simple recipe!",
            "datePublished": "2013-04-06T18:19:35.643Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Brandi"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Asparagus was on sale and in season at the grocery store yeah! This recipe was very good and oh so easy. I hadn't thought about putting balsalmic on asparagus but it was really good. I sprinkled some dried cranberries and pine nuts and tossed with the asparagus prior to baking just to jazz it up. Roasting with these additions turned out really nice. I think the olive oil was a little heavy and I think next time I'll use just 1 Tblsp. I also used a sheet pan suggested by another reviewer. I will make this again.",
            "datePublished": "2013-06-06T14:05:06.563Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Bren"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Easy and quick with ingredients that I usually have on hand. I cut the oil back to one tablespoon and roasted mine with fresh garlic for ten minutes as they were small. I added a few tablespoons of toasted pine nuts before serving for some extra crunch. I served this with pan seared salmon and Mushroom Orzo, also from this site.",
            "datePublished": "2016-04-11T16:28:23.117Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Baking Nana"
            },
            "reviewBody": "What is not to like? Asparagus and balsamic were just meant to go together. I fine dusting of Parmesan cheese would be great with this. I roasted on a sheet pan, at 400 for 10 minutes. Perfect!",
            "datePublished": "2012-06-22T08:46:42.760Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "DREGINEK"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Pretty good. Did on a sheet pan vs baking dish and I added some minced garlic. Used balsamic glaze/finishing sauce vs balsamic vinegar and a little less since it’s “thicker” in consistency. Simple, familiar flavor but still pretty good. And a breeze to pull together when you need to focus on main dish entrees. Thank you Gemini26!",
            "datePublished": "2023-05-07T02:14:50.457Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "KANDIYOHIV"
            },
            "reviewBody": "It was good but I think next time I'd add some garlic while roasting and/or add some soy sauce along with the vinegar. The balsamic wasn't quite strong enough on its own for me so I might also try a balsamic reduction.",
            "datePublished": "2013-03-26T16:45:27.957Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
